cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this result or these tools, please cite them as below."
title: "Moki&Julio: No symmetric 12-face Szilassi polyhedron - a computer-assisted proof with DRAT certificates"
authors:
  - name: "Moki&Julio"
date-released: 2026-09-27
version: "1.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Hashirama1337s/szilassi-12"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - Szilassi polyhedron
  - neighbourly polyhedra
  - polyhedral embedding
  - oriented matroids
  - SAT
  - DRAT proof
  - computer-assisted proof
  - genus 6
abstract: >-
  No polyhedron with 12 faces in which every two faces share an edge has a non-trivial symmetry. Such a polyhedron
  would be the dual of one of the 59 neighbourly 12-vertex triangulations of the genus-6 surface. For every map and
  every compatible symmetry group, the existence of a symmetric embedded realisation is encoded as a rank-4
  oriented-matroid SAT instance; all 36 instances are unsatisfiable, each with a DRAT proof checked by drat-trim, and an
  independently derived second encoding agrees on every case it completed. The asymmetric case remains open; the
  encoders, both exact embeddedness checkers, the certificate table and a one-command reproduction script are included.
